pve-fcsan (1.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New array drivers, each checked against the vendor's own SDK/tooling:
    - Dell PowerStore (PyPowerStore)
    - Dell PowerMax / VMAX via Unisphere (PyU4V): host group, storage group
      and masking view per cluster
    - NetApp ONTAP (netapp.ontap Ansible collection): FlexVol + LUN per
      datastore, one FCP igroup per cluster
    - NetApp E-Series (SANtricity Ansible collection)
    - Hitachi VSP via Configuration Manager REST (OpenStack Cinder hbsd):
      host group and LU path per target port
  * Vendor settings on arrays: system-id, svm, portgroup, srp, slo,
    target-ports.
  * Provisioning reads the WWID after mapping where the array only reports
    it then (Hitachi).

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.2.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Pure driver checked against Pure's generated SDK docs (FlashArray API 2.50):
    - POST /host-groups and /connections send a JSON body (fields optional)
    - free space from space.total_used (total_physical is deprecated)

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * InfiniBox driver checked against the InfiniSDK source:
    - unmap by LUN number (DELETE clusters/<id>/luns/lun/<n>), found via
      GET clusters/<id>?fields=luns; already unmapped is not an error
    - every non-GET request carries approved=true, as InfiniSDK sends it
    - FC ports are sent as type "fc"
    - paging also stops on number_of_objects or a short page

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Array drivers for Pure Storage FlashArray (REST 2.x, API token) and
    INFINIDAT InfiniBox (REST API), next to IBM Spectrum Virtualize.
  * Shared host / host-cluster registration logic in PVE::SAN::Array::Base.
  * Per-vendor defaults: API port, naming rules, recommended path policy.
  * GUI: array type picker adapts port, credentials and hints.

 -- pve-fcsan maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000

pve-fcsan (1.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Array integration (driver: IBM Spectrum Virtualize / FlashSystem REST API):
    add arrays with pinned TLS fingerprint, register the cluster as a host
    cluster, provision a datastore end to end (volume, map, rescan, datastore),
    grow on the array, delete including the array volume, link existing
    datastores.
  * GUI: Arrays tab, provisioning dialog, array-aware grow and delete.
  * CLI: pvesan array ..., pvesan provision, pvesan datastore array-grow.

